# Random modules whose predicates and lambda expressions are declared with
# random determinisms, committed choice ones among them, and whose goals
# call predicates of each determinism, committed choice ones among them,
# some without outputs (generate-switch-programs.py --determinism
# --committed). merkc must infer the determinisms of the procedures and
# their goals that mmc does, and report its determinism errors, those for
# committed choice calls where all solutions are wanted among them, at the
# same lines.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-switch-programs.py --determinism --committed --seed 2 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-switches --determinism %t/*.m
